-- title:
--   Drinfeld special fibre and level action on the blow-up chart
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume `hι`: there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with `hK`: $K=\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,L$ of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of that rational function field, the level being $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell)\,M'$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   Base ring and chart. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with $j$ equal, as a Laurent series, to the coefficient extension of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ with $u\in A^\times$ (`hϖt`). Write $C=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, $\mathfrak X=\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$ for the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two chart algebras, $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}:X_{\mathrm{Fin}}=\operatorname{Spec} C\to\mathfrak X$ and $\mathfrak X\to\operatorname{Spec} A$ for the canonical morphisms.
--
--   Supersingular centre. Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), supersingular in the sense `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point annihilated by $q$.
--
--   The uniform rigidity hypothesis `hArig` (seven clauses, summarised here). For every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$, every germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ from the base lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y')=z$ satisfying the same supersingularity condition as $y$ does, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\,C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v-fu\,)$, such that, with $\mathrm{toC}$ the completion map, $\mathrm{germY}$ the germ map $C\to\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ through $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ at $y'$, and $\mathrm{mkS}$ the quotient map: (i) $e$ carries the image of $a\in A$ to the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, in the sense [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, preserves $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, the restriction of such a $\tau$ to $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ as in (ii) acting trivially modulo $y'$, there are $\theta\in\mathrm{Aut}(S)$, $c\in W$ and $M\in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ intertwining $e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ with $\tau|_C$, $\theta$ fixing all constants, $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the images of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; (v) branch separation: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ with $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ and prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ each omitting one of the images of $X_0,X_1$, each containing $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e\circ\mathrm{toC}$ are distinct; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ with the same nondegeneracy, containing $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and containing $X_0+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and for $a\in C$: the germ of $a$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $q$-expansion of $j$ with $q$ replaced by $q^{q\ell}$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and for a suitable $a_0\in A$ with the difference lying in $y'$, there are $e_0\ge 1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is nonsingular in the sense that $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit whenever one of $a,b\in W$ is a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, and $e$ sends the germ of that difference to $\mathrm{mkS}\,h$.
--
--   The chosen chart. Fixed data $z,\varpi_z,y'$ as above with `hy'y`: $y'=y$, together with one witness $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1$ and the hypothesis `hW₁`, which asserts for this witness exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) listed above (with $W_1,\sigma_1,e_1$ in place of $W,\sigma,e$), in particular the Hasse-type coefficient criterion and the $\mathrm{jqNModC}$ clause.
--
--   The weighted centre and the blow-up chart. `hJ` pins $J$ to be the infimum of the set of ideals $J'$ of $C$ of the form $J'=(\tau|_C)^{-1}$ of the contraction along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t))$, $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0)$, $\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, as $\gamma$ runs over $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. `hB` pins $B$ to be the $A$-subalgebra $C[\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}]$ of $K$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and assume: `hR1`, that $C\le B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2`, that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; and `hR3` (five clauses), that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ if and only if $b\in\mathfrak m_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m_W\cap B$.
--
--   Conclusion. Five assertions hold.
--
--   (1) For every $\mathbb F_{q^2}=\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing}\,q\,k$, the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by $(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}\,q\,k-1)$, such that: $\rho$ is surjective; $\rho(b)=0$ if and only if $b\in\mathfrak m_W$; $\rho$ sends the image of $a\in A$ to the image of the residue of $a$; and for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ satisfying $f\in W\Leftrightarrow\tau f\in W$ for all $f\in K$, there exist a unit $c$ of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, the kernel of the character $(g,c)\mapsto\det(g)\,c^{q+1}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Z/q)\times\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$, such that: $\rho(\tau b)=\mathrm{hAction}\,q\,k\,(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)(\rho b)$ for every $b\in B$ with $\tau b\in B$; if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity then $c\neq 1$; and the same scalar occurs with trivial matrix part, namely there are $\gamma'\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, a level automorphism $\tau'$ at $\gamma'^{-1}$ preserving $W$, and a membership $(1,c)\in\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, with $\rho(\tau' b)=\mathrm{hAction}\,q\,k\,(1,c)(\rho b)$ for every $b\in B$ with $\tau' b\in B$.
--
--   (2) For every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\tau$ maps $B$ into $B$.
--
--   (3) For every prime ideal $Q$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$ there are $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ such that every $b\in B$ with $b\in\mathfrak m_W$ satisfies $\tau b\in B$ and $\tau b\in Q$.
--
--   (4) If $b\in B$ is such that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ the element $\tau b$, whenever it lies in $B$, lies in $\mathfrak m_W$, then the image of $\varpi$ in $B$ divides $b$.
--
--   (5) For every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$: if $\tau$ preserves $y$, in the sense that for $b\in C$ with $\tau b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ if and only if $\tau b\in y$, then $f\in W$ if and only if $\tau f\in W$, for all $f\in K$.
--
--   This is the equivariance step for the blown-up supersingular chart $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ over a henselian discrete valuation base: it identifies the special fibre of $B$ with the affine Drinfeld curve over the residue field, together with the action of the level automorphisms through the subgroup $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ and the transitivity and reducedness statements at the fibre over $\varpi$. It is used by the assembly result [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_supersingularAffineChart_ends_moduliHasse_commonChart_orbitPoles_inertia_chartAlgFin_of_stalk_drinfeldChart_moduliHasse_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_supersingularAffineChart_ends_moduliHasse_commonChart_orbitPoles_inertia_chartAlgFin_of_stalk_drinfeldChart_moduliHasse_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia), and rests on the completed-stalk Drinfeld presentation supplied by `hArig` and `hW₁`.
